      },
      "authorType": "TOPIC",
      "content": "<p>How to fix this ?</p>\n<p>[ERROR] Training error: CUDA error: no kernel image is available for execution on the device\nSearch for <code>cudaErrorNoKernelImageForDevice' in https://docs.nvidia.com/cuda/cuda-runtime-api/group__CUDART__TYPES.html for more information.\nCUDA kernel errors might be asynchronously reported at some other API call, so the stacktrace below might be incorrect.\nFor debugging consider passing CUDA_LAUNCH_BLOCKING=1\nCompile with</code>TORCH_USE_CUDA_DSA` to enable device-side assertions.</p>",
      "feedbackTrackingData": {},
      "id": 3423202,
      "isThankYou": false,
      "kernelVersion": 0,
      "parent": {},
      "postDate": "2026-03-18T09:17:13.103Z",
      "rawMarkdown": "How to fix this ?\n\n\n[ERROR] Training error: CUDA error: no kernel image is available for execution on the device\nSearch for `cudaErrorNoKernelImageForDevice' in https://docs.nvidia.com/cuda/cuda-runtime-api/group__CUDART__TYPES.html for more information.\nCUDA kernel errors might be asynchronously reported at some other API call, so the stacktrace below might be incorrect.\nFor debugging consider passing CUDA_LAUNCH_BLOCKING=1\nCompile with `TORCH_USE_CUDA_DSA` to enable device-side assertions.\n",
